ted as ‘inapplicable’ by individual Majors/Departments. - 6.Notices - 1) Courses with a grade of C- or lower are listed as U, and credits arenot recognizedas earned credits - 2) Courses completed by S/U evaluationcannot be acknowledged as Teacher Training courses. - 3) Courses selected for S/U evaluation are excluded when calculating the criteria for receiving the highest/high honor roll - - Students with less than 15 credits per semester after excluding the courses with S/U evaluation are not eligible for the highest/high honor roll for the relevant semester. - 4) Students who received a U grade in the S/U evaluation courses are not eligible for the relevant semester's highest/high honor roll. - 5) Courses Grade selected for S/U evaluation are reflected as original letter grades when screening Korea Student Aid Foundation scholarships - 6) Please check the attached S/U Evaluation Guidelines before applying. - 교 무 처     학 사 지 원 팀 - Academic Support Team, Office of Academic Affairs

